On Sun, May 31, 2015 at 3:14 PM, Spheniscine (la zipcpi) <
spheniscine@gmail.com> wrote:

> You can use the lerfu "mu bu" and "ci bu".
>>
>
> That would make digit-heavy character-strings extremely clunky. Besides,
> if we're going to have to define a new selma'o anyway to retain
> compatibility, it might as well be MEhO.
>

Or just use "lo'u" if what we want is just a string of characters without
any internal grammar. But li/me'o take a mathematical expression, not just
any character-string, one returns an expression and the other returns its
value. It would be strange for them to have different grammars, because
then you couldn't distinguish the value from expression by just choosing
"li" or "me'o".

mu'o mi'e xorxes

